,1)$?","options":["$\\pi$","$-\\pi/2$","$\\pi/2$","$0$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"95a00d079738f0d54e2639bb","time_limit":40},{"id":"expansion_2_argument_arctangent_013","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which case of $\\operatorname{atan2}(y,x)$ applies when $x \\lt 0$ and $y\\ge0$?","options":["$\\arctan(y/x)-\\pi$","$\\pi/2$","Undefined","$\\arctan(y/x)+\\pi$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"4faf70f79b504b7ee4fcd3f2","time_limit":20},{"id":"expansion_2_argument_arctangent_014","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which case of $\\operatorname{atan2}(y,x)$ applies when $x \\lt 0$ and $y \\lt 0$?","options":["$\\arctan(y/x)+\\pi$","$-\\pi/2$","$0$","$\\arctan(y/x)-\\pi$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"6d9ba3010477ec0205bedb60","time_limit":20},{"id":"expansion_2_argument_arctangent_015","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Why is $\\operatorname{atan2}$ better suited than $\\arctan(y/x)$ for locating an angle?","options":["It uses the coordinate ratio and ignores both coordinate signs.","It distinguishes quadrants and treats vertical directions separately.","It is defined only when the horizontal coordinate is positive.","It always returns the representative in the interval $[0,2\\pi)$."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"a7a95ae7207b34f0d75aa225","time_limit":30},{"id":"expansion_2_argument_arctangent_016","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"What is $\\operatorname{atan2}(1,1)$?","options":["$3\\pi/4$","$-\\pi/4$","$\\pi/4$","$-3\\pi/4$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"fee23b5f98863fcf3aac72c1","time_limit":20},{"id":"expansion_2_argument_arctangent_017","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"What is $\\operatorname{atan2}(-1,1)$?","options":["$\\pi/4$","$3\\pi/4$","$-3\\pi/4$","$-\\pi/4$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"a34857a356e561493928b37e","time_limit